    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class (the other two files are `AcceptanceBase` and a support class). Build is green.\n\nDone. The change rejects creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by another owner, responding with 409.\n\nWhat I added, following the existing telephone-unique pattern:\n\n- **`CheckOwnerEmailUnique`** (`.../function/owner/`) \u2014 a pipeline step that reads the validated `OwnerFieldsDto`, and (email being optional) skips when absent; otherwise compares the lower-cased email against every existing owner's email and throws a checked `OwnerEmailInUseException` on a match.\n- **`OwnerEmailInUseException`** \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause for escalation.\n- **`OwnerEmailInUseExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `409 Conflict`.\n- **`officefloor/escalation/...OwnerEmailInUseException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `checkEmail` step (under `transaction` governance) between `checkTelephone` and `checkHousehold`, so a duplicate email is a 409 before any record is persisted.\n\nThe new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test and the full suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
